{"body": "Licensed Child Care Licensed Child Care Center Maximum Rate Center Maximum Rate Licensed Family Child Licensed Family Child Care Maximum Rate Care Maximum Rate License-Exempt Child License-Exempt Child Care Maximum Rate Care Maximum Rate Maine Department of Health and Human Services Child Care Market Rates May 19, 2025 COUNTY\n\nLicensed Child Care Licensed Child Care Center Maximum Rate Center Maximum Rate Licensed Family Child Licensed Family Child Care Maximum Rate Care Maximum Rate License-Exempt Child License-Exempt Child Care Maximum Rate Care Maximum Rate COUNTY\n\nLicensed Child Care Licensed Child Care Center Maximum Rate Center Maximum Rate Licensed Family Child Licensed Family Child Care Maximum Rate Care Maximum Rate License-Exempt Child License-Exempt Child Care Maximum Rate Care Maximum Rate Infant: A child six (6) weeks of age through twelve (12) months of age Toddler: A child aged twelve (12) months plus one (1) day through thirty-six (36) months of age Preschool: A child aged three (3) years plus one day to age five (5), who has not yet entered kindergarten School: A child five (5) years plus one day or older in full day schooling, up to thirteen (13) years of age. If a child has documented special needs, the end date goes up to nineteen (19) years of age Age Definitons Hour Definitions Full time: 30-50 hours weekly Part time: 1-29 hours weekly COUNTY", "citation_label": "Maine: Maine Child Care Market Rates (maximum rates by county and setting), May 19, 2025 1", "citation_path": "us-me/policy/ccdf/rate-schedules/child-care-market-rates-2025-05-19/document-1", "document_class": "policy", "expression_date": "2025-05-19", "id": "ac865186-486e-5f1c-a4ef-d4af8cd76dc4", "jurisdiction": "us-me", "kind": "document", "language": "en", "level": 2, "metadata": {"block_count": 1, "closure_elements": ["ccdf-s30"], "content_type": "application/pdf", "discovered_via": "manual-review:ccdf-agent-queue additional_families; index https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/