{"body": "Individuals eligible for child care subsidy from the Department of Health and Human Services, Child Care Affordability Program must comply with income eligibility criteria below.\n\nFunds | State Funds (SPSS) Fund for a Healthy Maine (FHM) Child Care Development Funds (CCDF) Temporary Assistance to Needy Families (TANF) Income Eligibility | All families must meet income guidelines of gross family income at or below 125% Fee Assessment | Fees are assessed to all families.", "citation_label": "Maine: CCAP Current Income Guidelines (125% SMI), April 18, 2026 1", "citation_path": "us-me/policy/ccdf/rate-schedules/ccap-income-guidelines-2026-04-18/block-1", "document_class": "policy", "expression_date": "2026-04-18", "heading": "INCOME ELIGIBLITY CRITERIA (125% SMI)", "id": "2c4dd103-4e93-5388-b041-3ec6a62ff924", "jurisdiction": "us-me", "kind": "block", "language": "en", "level": 2, "metadata": {"block_count": 2, "closure_elements": ["ccdf-s30"], "content_type": "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document", "discovered_via": "manual-review:ccdf-agent-queue additional_families; index https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/ocfs/provider-resources/child-care-subsidy-information-for-providers", "document_subtype": "rate_or_copay_schedule", "download_url": "https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/sites/maine.gov.dhhs/files/inline-files/4.18.26%20125%20CCAP%20income%20guidelines.docx", "kind": "block", "primary_source": true, "program": "CCDF", "publisher_index_url": "https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/ocfs/provider-resources/child-care-subsidy-information-for-providers", "source_authority": "Maine DHHS Office of Child and Family Services, Child Care Affordability Program (CCAP)", "source_discovery_group": "us-me/policy/ccdf", "source_note": "posted as a Word document; the page labels the link (PDF)", "title": "Maine: CCAP Current Income Guidelines (125% SMI), April 18, 2026"}, "ordinal": 1, "parent_citation_path": "us-me/policy/ccdf/rate-schedules/ccap-income-guidelines-2026-04-18", "parent_id": "406b3a13-5b66-5c6b-a273-ef528cee8566", "source_as_of": "2026-09-13", "source_format": "docx", "source_id": "us-me-ccdf-rate-schedule-ccap-income-guidelines-2026-04-18", "source_path": "sources/us-me/policy/2026-09-13-ccdf-rate-schedules/official-documents/us-me-ccdf-rate-schedule-ccap-income-guidelines-2026-04-18.docx", "source_url": "https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/sites/maine.gov.dhhs/files/inline-files/4.18.26%20125%20CCAP%20income%20guidelines.docx", "version": "2026-09-13-ccdf-rate-schedules"}
{"body": "FAMILY SIZE | ANNUAL INCOME | MONTHLY INCOME (ANNUAL/12) | WEEKLY INCOME (ANNUAL/4.3) 1 | $76,742.25 | $6,395.19 | $1487.25 2 | $100,355.25 | $8,362.94 | $1944.87 3 | $123,968.25 | $10,330.69 | $2402.49 4 | $147,581.25 | $12,298.44 | $2860.10 5 | $171,194.25 | $14,266.19 | $3317.72 6 | $194,807.25 | $16,233.94 | $3775.33 7 | $199,234.69 | $16,602.89 | $3861.14 8 | $203,662.13 | $16,971.84 | $3946.94 9 | $208,089.56 | $17,340.80 | $4032.74 10 | $212,517.00 | $17,709.75 | $4118.55\n\nAdd 3% for additional family members. For families with more than one child in care, the youngest child is always considered the first child enrolled. The total amount of assessed fees to a family shall not exceed 10% of the family\u2019s gross income for all of their children.\n\nWeekly fee assessments must be rounded down to the nearest dollar. All assessed parent fees shall be paid directly to the caregiver by the parent.\n\nSMI DATA: https://acf.gov/sites/default/files/documents/ocs/COMM_LIHEAP_IM2025-02_SMIStateTable_Att4.pdf", "citation_label": "Maine: CCAP Current Income Guidelines (125% SMI), April 18, 2026 2", "citation_path": "us-me/policy/ccdf/rate-schedules/ccap-income-guidelines-2026-04-18/block-2", "document_class": "policy", "expression_date": "2026-04-18", "heading": "Effective 4/18/2026", "id": "474ae56a-24a5-5979-b281-69de2bdae4ae", "jurisdiction": "us-me", "kind": "block", "language": "en", "level": 2, "metadata": {"block_count": 2, "closure_elements": ["ccdf-s30"], "content_type": "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document", "discovered_via": "manual-review:ccdf-agent-queue additional_families; index https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/ocfs/provider-resources/child-care-subsidy-information-for-providers", "document_subtype": "rate_or_copay_schedule", "download_url": "https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/sites/maine.gov.dhhs/files/inline-files/4.18.26%20125%20CCAP%20income%20guidelines.docx", "kind": "block", "primary_source": true, "program": "CCDF